ttps://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"> I'm also confused by this. Are you asking if the acceptance test results listed in the PR body are running the tests or skipping them?\r\n\r\nSorry, I think you intuited what I meant. 😅\r\n\r\nI had trouble understanding how they could all pass but be committed such that they are skipped, but I also wondered what circumstances we would want to run them.","created_at":"2025-03-07T21:45:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T21:45:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985751367","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/10513","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985751367"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985751367"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/10513"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985751367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1983478028,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985752956","pull_request_review_id":2668453119,"id":1985752956,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc52XC98","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@\n+skip 'it creates a fork owned by the user running the test'\n+\n+# Setup environment variables used for testscript\n+env REPO=${SCRIPT_NAME}-${RANDOM_STRING}\n+env FORK=${REPO}-fork\n+\n+# Use gh as a credential helper\n+exec gh auth setup-git\n+\n+# Get the current username for the fork owner\n+exec gh api user --jq .login\n+stdout2env USER\n+\n+# Create a repository to act as upstream with a file so it has a default branch\n+exec gh repo create ${ORG}/${REPO} --add-readme --private\n+\n+# Defer repo cleanup of upstream\n+defer gh repo delete --yes ${ORG}/${REPO}\n+\n+# Create a user fork of repository. This will be owned by USER.\n+exec gh repo fork ${ORG}/${REPO} --fork-name ${FORK}\n+\n+# Defer repo cleanup of fork\n+defer gh repo delete --yes ${USER}/${FORK}\n+sleep 5\n+exec gh repo view ${USER}/${FORK} --json id --jq '.id'\n+stdout2env FORK_ID\n+\n+# Clone the repo\n+exec gh repo clone ${USER}/${FORK}\n+cd ${FORK}\n+\n+# Configure default push behavior so local and remote branches will be the same\n+exec git config push.default current","path":"acceptance/testdata/pr/pr-create-respects-push-destination.txtar","commit_id":"a9dbda69135631511eebfa8173f80e93e726c7b2","original_commit_id":"dde7e24847970df859ca883ba316b4e09d039a71","user":{"login":"andyfeller","id":2089743,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODk3NDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2089743?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller","html_url":"https://github.com/andyfeller","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"Sorry, let me rephrase 😅\r\n\r\n> Does `exec git config push.default current` actually set the value?  Or is this missing `set` argument?","created_at":"2025-03-07T21:47:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T21:47:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985752956","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/10513","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985752956"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985752956"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/10513"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985752956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":36,"original_line":36,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1983497480,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":34,"position":36,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985782446","pull_request_review_id":2668504716,"id":1985782446,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc52XKKu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@\n+skip 'it creates a fork owned by the user running the test'\n+\n+# Setup environment variables used for testscript\n+env REPO=${SCRIPT_NAME}-${RANDOM_STRING}\n+env FORK=${REPO}-fork\n+\n+# Use gh as a credential helper\n+exec gh auth setup-git\n+\n+# Get the current username for the fork owner\n+exec gh api user --jq .login\n+stdout2env USER\n+\n+# Create a repository to act as upstream with a file so it has a default branch\n+exec gh repo create ${ORG}/${REPO} --add-readme --private\n+\n+# Defer repo cleanup of upstream\n+defer gh repo delete --yes ${ORG}/${REPO}\n+\n+# Create a user fork of repository. This will be owned by USER.\n+exec gh repo fork ${ORG}/${REPO} --fork-name ${FORK}\n+\n+# Defer repo cleanup of fork\n+defer gh repo delete --yes ${USER}/${FORK}\n+sleep 5\n+exec gh repo view ${USER}/${FORK} --json id --jq '.id'\n+stdout2env FORK_ID\n+\n+# Clone the repo\n+exec gh repo clone ${USER}/${FORK}\n+cd ${FORK}\n+\n+# Configure default push behavior so local and remote branches will be the same\n+exec git config push.default current","path":"acceptance/testdata/pr/pr-create-respects-push-destination.txtar","commit_id":"a9dbda69135631511eebfa8173f80e93e726c7b2","original_commit_id":"dde7e24847970df859ca883ba316b4e09d039a71","user":{"login":"andyfeller","id":2089743,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODk3NDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2089743?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller","html_url":"https://github.com/andyfeller","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"Cool story, apparently @BagToad and I discovered `git config` will actually imply `set` in this situation and magically work!\r\n\r\nIt isn't documented in [`git config` docs](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config) and we haven't been using it until now, so going to ignore this for this PR.","created_at":"2025-03-07T22:15:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T22:15:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985782446","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/10513","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985782446"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985782446"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/10513"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985782446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":36,"original_line":36,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1983497480,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":34,"position":36,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985783557","pull_request_review_id":2668506406,"id":1985783557,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc52XKcF","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@\n+skip 'it creates a fork owned by the user running the test'\n+\n+# Setup environment variables used for testscript\n+env REPO=${SCRIPT_NAME}-${RANDOM_STRING}\n+env FORK=${REPO}-fork\n+\n+# Use gh as a credential helper\n+exec gh auth setup-git\n+\n+# Get the current username for the fork owner\n+exec gh api user --jq .login\n+stdout2env USER\n+\n+# Create a repository to act as upstream with a file so it has a default branch\n+exec gh repo create ${ORG}/${REPO} --add-readme --private\n+\n+# Defer repo cleanup of upstream\n+defer gh repo delete --yes ${ORG}/${REPO}\n+\n+# Create a user fork of repository. This will be owned by USER.\n+exec gh repo fork ${ORG}/${REPO} --fork-name ${FORK}\n+\n+# Defer repo cleanup of fork\n+defer gh repo delete --yes ${USER}/${FORK}\n+sleep 5\n+exec gh repo view ${USER}/${FORK} --json id --jq '.id'\n+stdout2env FORK_ID\n+\n+# Clone the repo\n+exec gh repo clone ${USER}/${FORK}\n+cd ${FORK}\n+\n+# Prepare a branch where changes are pulled from the upstream default branch but pushed to fork\n+exec git checkout -b feature-branch upstream/main\n+exec git config branch.feature-branch.pushRemote origin","path":"acceptance/testdata/pr/pr-create-respects-branch-pushremote.txtar","commit_id":"a9dbda69135631511eebfa8173f80e93e726c7b2","original_commit_id":"dde7e24847970df859ca883ba316b4e09d039a71","user":{"login":"andyfeller","id":2089743,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODk3NDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2089743?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller","html_url":"https://github.com/andyfeller","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andyfeller/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"Closing this for the same reason as https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985782446","created_at":"2025-03-07T22:16:50Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T22:16:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985783557","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/10513","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments/1985783557"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/10513#discussion_r1985783557"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/p